{"id":"ffset.1","n":"ffset","s":"1","src":{"r":{"pkg":"linuxconsoletools","ver":"1.7.1-3.el9","repo":"AppStream","url":"https://dl.rockylinux.org/vault/rocky/9.6/AppStream/x86_64/os/Packages/l/linuxconsoletools-1.7.1-3.el9.x86_64.rpm","path":"/usr/share/man/man1/ffset.1.gz","sha256":"3311bbbf4dea96d94ece964434224ac9ff49dc4ef1a83194011ffe3091ebe584","date":"March 8, 2009","origin":"ffset"}},"nopt":{"r":2},"desc":"set force-feedback device parameters","r":[["NAME","<p>ffset - set force-feedback device parameters</p>"],["SYNOPSIS","<p><b>ffset</b> &lt;<i>device</i>&gt; [<b>-g</b> &lt;<i>gain</i>&gt;] [<b>-a</b> &lt;<i>autocenter strength</i>&gt;]</p>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p>ffset sets the gain and autocenter strength of a force-feedback device.</p>"],["OPTIONS","<dl><dt>&lt;<i>device</i>&gt;</dt><dd>The device to configure.</dd><dt data-o=\"\"><b>-g</b> &lt;<i>gain</i>&gt;</dt><dd>The gain (0-100).</dd><dt data-o=\"\"><b>-a</b> &lt;<i>autocenter strength</i>&gt;</dt><dd>The autocenter strength (0-100).</dd></dl>"],["SEE ALSO","<p><b>ffcfstress</b>(1), <b>ffmvforce</b>(1), <b>fftest</b>(1), <b>jscal</b>(1), <b>jstest</b>(1).</p>"],["AUTHOR","<p><b>ffset</b> was written by Johann Deneux.</p> <p>This manual page was written by Stephen Kitt &lt;steve@sk2.org&gt;, for the Debian GNU/Linux system (but may be used by others). It was last modified for <b>ffmvforce</b> dated May 30, 2001.</p>"]]}